Falsifies `usb::verification::the_header_parsers_are_total`.

The defect: `DeviceDescriptor::parse` loses its length check and indexes `bytes[0]` of whatever it is handed, so an
empty or short descriptor from the device is an out-of-bounds read.

Expected to fail: the bounds check on `bytes[0]` in `DeviceDescriptor::parse`.

diff --git a/src/descriptor.rs b/src/descriptor.rs
--- a/src/descriptor.rs
+++ b/src/descriptor.rs
@@ -141,9 +141,6 @@
     /// }
     /// ```
     pub fn parse(bytes: &[u8]) -> Result<DeviceDescriptor, DescriptorError> {
-        if bytes.len() < DEVICE_DESCRIPTOR_BYTES {
-            return Err(DescriptorError::Truncated);
-        }
         if (bytes[0] as usize) < DEVICE_DESCRIPTOR_BYTES || bytes[1] != DEVICE {
             return Err(DescriptorError::NotThatDescriptor);
         }
